# WHAT THE `v12` BUILD CONTEXT SENDS, and it is an ALLOWLIST on purpose.
#
# W71917 widened `Dockerfile.claude`'s context from `v12/worker` to `v12`,
# because the image now needs the distribution's `source_profiles` package
# beside the worker modules and a context cannot reach above itself. That is
# correct and it has three consequences this file answers.
#
# FIRST, AND THE ONE THAT ACTUALLY BIT: a context is TARRED AS IT IS READ, and
# `v12/python` is a directory the test suite writes into while it runs. A
# whole-tree run builds this image while other cases are creating and removing
# temporary trees under that path, and the build failed there while passing
# every time it was run on its own. A denylist cannot fix that — it would have
# to name every transient thing a suite might make — so this excludes
# EVERYTHING and re-includes exactly the two directories the recipe copies.
# Nothing else can appear in the context, so nothing else can change under it.
#
# SECOND, COST. The old context was four files; the whole distribution is
# nominally in this one and only two directories are ever copied from it.
#
# THIRD, byte-code caches must not travel. W85497 is the record of what they
# cost — a verifier that created 149 cache paths inflated a proposal past
# reviewability — and a cache built by the host's interpreter landing in an
# image with a different one is a second copy of that mistake, made at build
# time instead of at run time.
#
# ORDER IS THE MECHANISM: later patterns win, so the re-includes come before
# the cache exclusions that carve into them.
*
!worker
!python/src/baton_v12/source_profiles

# Not even inside the two directories above.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
